# Social Media Post Automation

An n8n-based social media content posting automation that processes user-created posts and prepares them for publishing across multiple social media platforms.

## Overview

This automation allows users to submit a post title and content through a simple web form. The workflow receives the submitted data through an n8n webhook and processes the selected posting mode.

The workflow supports:

- Post title and content submission
- ALL platforms mode
- SPECIFIC platform selection mode
- Facebook
- Instagram
- X (Twitter)
- LinkedIn
- Platform-specific workflow routing
- Post-ready output generation

## Workflow

The automation follows this general process:

Webhook
→ Posting Mode Check
→ Platform Selection
→ Platform Processing
→ Post Ready Output

## Supported Platforms

- Facebook
- Instagram
- X (Twitter)
- LinkedIn

## Features

### 1. Webhook Input

The workflow receives post information from the web form through an n8n webhook.

### 2. Posting Mode

The user can select:

- ALL – process the post for all supported platforms
- SPECIFIC – process the post only for selected platforms

### 3. Platform Routing

Conditional nodes determine which platforms should process the submitted post.

### 4. Post Preparation

Each selected platform receives a platform-specific processing step that prepares the post data for publishing.

## Technology Stack

- n8n
- Node.js
- JavaScript
- HTML/CSS/JavaScript
- Webhooks

## Current Status

The workflow has been tested successfully for webhook input, posting mode detection, platform selection, and post-ready processing.

Actual social media publishing requires connecting the appropriate platform APIs and authentication credentials.

